        ],
        "page_range": "658",
        "body_preview": "In the transmit direction a host outputs a compliant electrical signal, and a compliant module, when receiving the compliant electrical signal, transmits a compliant optical output signal on the medium. In the receive direction, a compliant module, when receiving a compliant optical input, delivers a compliant electrical output signal to the host. A compliant host, when receiving a compliant electrical signal from a compliant module, delivers the specified raw BER to the subsequent FEC decoder.…",
        "body_text": "In the transmit direction a host outputs a compliant electrical signal, and a compliant\nmodule, when receiving the compliant electrical signal, transmits a compliant optical\noutput signal on the medium. In the receive direction, a compliant module, when\nreceiving a compliant optical input, delivers a compliant electrical output signal to the\nhost. A compliant host, when receiving a compliant electrical signal from a compliant\nmodule, delivers the specified raw BER to the subsequent FEC decoder. Error bursts\nwith length more than 130 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder shall occur\nwith a probability of less than 1 in 1020 PAM4 symbols. To enable a more practical test,\nerror bursts with length more than 66 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder\nshould occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1012 PAM4 symbols. Optical\ncompliance is typically set by another specification and error performance may also be\nset by another specification. Unless otherwise specified, a raw Bit Error Ratio (BER)\nbetter than or equal to 2.0x10-4 may be required provided that the error statistics are\nsufficiently random to meet the system requirements. The interface BER is the average\nof the BER across a group of lanes that share a FEC decoder. The impairments of both\nthe optical and electrical interfaces cause errors at the host receiver. See also\nAppendix 16.D.",
        "role": "technical"
      },
      "added_snippets": [
        "In the transmit direction a host outputs a compliant electrical signal, and a compliant module, when receiving the compliant electrical signal, transmits a compliant optical output signal on the medium. In the receive direction, a compliant module, when receiving a compliant optical input, delivers a compliant electrical output signal to the host. A compliant host, when receiving a compliant electrical signal from a compliant module, delivers the specified raw BER to the subsequent FEC decoder. Error bursts with length more than 130 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder shall occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1020 PAM4 symbols. To enable a more practical test, error bursts with length more than 66 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder should occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1012 PAM4 symbols. Optical compliance is typically set by another specification and error performance may also be set by another specification. Unless otherwise specified, a raw Bit Error Ratio (BER) better than or equal to 2.0x10-4 may be required provided that the error statistics are sufficiently random to meet the system requirements. The interface BER is the average of the BER across a group of lanes that share a FEC decoder. The impairments of both the optical and electrical interfaces cause errors at the host receiver.",
        "See also Appendix 16.D."
      ],
      "original_display_added_snippets": [
        "In the transmit direction a host outputs a compliant electrical signal, and a compliant module, when receiving the compliant electrical signal, transmits a compliant optical output signal on the medium. In the receive direction, a compliant module, when receiving a compliant optical input, delivers a compliant electrical output signal to the host. A compliant host, when receiving a compliant electrical signal from a compliant module, delivers the specified raw BER to the subsequent FEC decoder. Error bursts with length more than 130 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder shall occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1020 PAM4 symbols. To enable a more practical test, error bursts with length more than 66 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder should occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1012 PAM4 symbols. Optical compliance is typically set by another specification and error performance may also be set by another specification. Unless otherwise specified, a raw Bit Error Ratio (BER) better than or equal to 2.0x10-4 may be required provided that the error statistics are sufficiently random to meet the system requirements. The interface BER is the average of the BER across a group of lanes that share a FEC decoder. The impairments of both the optical and electrical interfaces cause errors at the host receiver.",
        "See also Appendix 16.D."
